+## Economy in the room (§11, §16, `economy-online`)
+
+- **Supply crates.** `supplySites(map)` (`supply.ts`, pure) puts one crate halfway along each island's route to the hub, clear of docks, spawns and test lanes and 20 tiles apart; their ids are the ledger's supply caches. Each tick in play, after the encounters, an unclaimed crate a ship's hull touches goes to the lowest player id touching it (`crateClaims`): `grantGold` (`supply-cache`, 25 once). Crates are filtered by sight, and a claimed one leaves every view.
+- **Shop** (protocol v11). `buy-tonic` and `use-tonic` carry a request id; a `ShopBook` per kind answers decided ids again (`replayed`), merges a pending one, refuses a third `busy`. After the claim step each tick takes one of each per player: a purchase needs the ship moored at a dock on that tick (else `not-at-dock`), then the ledger's `purchase` decides it under `tonic:<id>`; the rumor on the shelf is the journal's `buy-rumor`, charged under `rumor:<id>`, so one client id is two purchases. Requests still waiting at the end are answered (`match-ended`, `not-in-play`); a rumor id retried for another type is `duplicate`.
+- **Tonic.** `useTonic` gets `atSea` and `grappled` (defender of a grapple windup); a reservation or duel is `player-in-duel`. Drunk on tick t, `drinkTonic` sets the ship's `tonicUntil` = t + 240: the steps of ticks t + 1 to t + 240 cap speed at 39 + `tonicSpeedBonus` (maxSpeed / 10 rounded = 43), and each step clamps to its cap, so t + 241 is 39 again. It is in the simulation state and hash; a test replays the room's recorded inputs and drinks to its hash. A lost duel keeps tonics.
+- **Visibility and browser.** Gold, `tonics`, `tonicUntil` and `maxSpeed` sit in the player's own status; answers go to the sender only. B opens `ShopPanel` when moored (casting off or a grapple closes it); T sends one `use-tonic` per press; the purse shows the timer, the HUD `data-max-speed`. Branch table: `docs/economy-online-coverage.md`.
